meta {
  name: Submit CSV Import (Stream)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{backendUrl}}/api/csv/submit/stream
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  [
    {
      "title": "Elden Ring",
      "genre": "RPG",
      "platform": ["PC"],
      "status": "In Progress",
      "owned": true
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  SSE submit (media_type: text/event-stream) - Bruno's plain HTTP
  request type will just return the raw event-stream body once the
  connection closes, not live progress. Creates one backlog entry per
  confirmed preview row from "Preview CSV Import (Stream)" - the body
  is the client-confirmed row list, nothing is recomputed server-side.
  Run auth/Login first.

  Emits a `progress` event per row processed, then a `done` event
  carrying {created: BacklogEntryResponse[], skipped: [{title,
  reason}]} - a per-row failure (e.g. a duplicate steam_app_id, or a
  field exceeding its DB column length) is skipped rather than failing
  the whole submit, and reported back with its title and reason
  instead of only being logged server-side.
}
